        "input": "random_index from /dev/urandom",
        "operation": "FREE msg[random_idx] then swap msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_idx] without nulling the old last slot",
        "risk": "HIGH",
        "reason": "After free(msg[random_idx]), the code copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_idx] and decrements cookie_num, but msg[cookie_num-1] (the old last slot) is NOT nulled out. The freed pointer remains in the msg array at the old last index, which is now == cookie_num (one past the new valid range). This is a potential UAF/dangling pointer if the index can reach that slot."
      },
      {
        "function": "edit_cookie",
        "input": "index from scanf(%llu)",
        "operation": "WRITE to msg[index] with read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)",
        "risk": "HIGH",
        "reason": "The index check uses signed comparison 'jl' (index < cookie_num) where index is loaded as unsigned 64-bit but compared with signed jl. A negative value (high bit set) would pass the signed comparison and allow indexing into msg[] at a negative offset, potentially reaching memory before the msg array. Additionally, if the freed slot from eat_cookie can be accessed, this writes to a freed heap chunk."
      },
